    "q-97660": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97660",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $80$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store has neither the first $3$ issues nor the final issue in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the probability that he chooses either issue $20$ or issue $23?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the issue Jack selects. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{4,5,…,79\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(X=20\\,\\,or\\,\\,X=23).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{4,5,…,79\\},$ and the set $S=\\{4,5,…,79\\}$ has $|S|=79-4+1=76$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{76}, & x=4,5,…,79 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy the given condition are $20,23.$ There are $2$ of these elements. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=20\\,\\,or\\,\\,X=23)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{76}=\\frac{1}{38}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97660-a",
              "type": "math",
